CORE
deduction.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ deduced: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ auto, decltype, value-initialized: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ trait: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [temp.deduct.type]/8 (`T C::*'), [dcl.spec.auto], [dcl.type.decltype],
[dcl.init.general]/9 (value-initialization gives the null member pointer
value): pointers to data members through template argument deduction,
auto, decltype and a partial specialization on `T C::*'.  g++ 13 and
clang++ 18 accept the program.
